    {
      "atom_id": "A2.SS2.SSS3.2",
      "section": "A2.SS2.SSS3",
      "kind": "proof-container",
      "raw_locator": "#A2.SS2.SSS3.2",
      "source_text": "Proof of Lemma 3.3 . Let $a$ denote the single-block Hellinger affinity: $a:=\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{n}}\\sqrt{p_{+1}(x)p_{-1}(x)}\\,dx.$ Cauchy–Schwarz and $\\int p_{+1}=\\int p_{-1}=1$ give $0\\leq a\\leq 1$ and $\\displaystyle\\operatorname{TV}(P_{+1},P_{-1})$ $\\displaystyle=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{n}}|\\sqrt{p_{+1}}-\\sqrt{p_{-1}}|(\\sqrt{p_{+1}}+\\sqrt{p_{-1}})$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{n}}(\\sqrt{p_{+1}}-\\sqrt{p_{-1}})^{2}\\right)^{1/2}\\left(\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{n}}(\\sqrt{p_{+1}}+\\sqrt{p_{-1}})^{2}\\right)^{1/2}$ $\\displaystyle=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{(2-2a)(2+2a)}=\\sqrt{1-a^{2}}.$ Proposition B.7 therefore implies $a\\leq\\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{4}e^{-10n/\\sqrt{\\kappa}}}\\leq\\exp\\left\\{-\\frac{1}{8}e^{-10n/\\sqrt{\\kappa}}\\right\\},$ (25) where the last inequality follows from $\\log(1-t)\\leq-t$ for $0\\leq t<1$ . Let $\\bar{p}_{b}$ be the density of $\\bar{\\pi}_{b}$ . When $kn<d$ , write $\\varphi_{d-kn}$ for the standard Gaussian density on $\\mathbb{R}^{d-kn}$ . By Eq. ( 6 ), $\\bar{p}_{b}(x_{1},\\ldots,x_{k},z)=\\prod_{j=1}^{k}p_{b}(x_{j})\\,\\varphi_{d-kn}(z).$ Tonelli’s theorem and $\\int\\varphi_{d-kn}=1$ give $\\displaystyle\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{d}}\\sqrt{\\bar{p}_{+1}(x)\\bar{p}_{-1}(x)}\\,dx$ $\\displaystyle=\\prod_{j=1}^{k}\\left(\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{n}}\\sqrt{p_{+1}(x_{j})p_{-1}(x_{j})}\\,dx_{j}\\right)\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{d-kn}}\\varphi_{d-kn}(z)\\,dz$ $\\displaystyle=a^{k}.$ When $kn=d$ , the same identity holds with the Gaussian factor omitted. Finally, $\\min\\{u,v\\}\\leq\\sqrt{uv}$ for $u,v\\geq 0$ implies $\\displaystyle\\operatorname{TV}(\\bar{\\pi}_{+1},\\bar{\\pi}_{-1})$ $\\displaystyle=1-\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{d}}\\min\\{\\bar{p}_{+1}(x),\\bar{p}_{-1}(x)\\}\\,dx$ $\\displaystyle\\geq 1-\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{d}}\\sqrt{\\bar{p}_{+1}(x)\\bar{p}_{-1}(x)}\\,dx$ $\\displaystyle=1-a^{k}$ $\\displaystyle\\geq 1-\\exp\\left\\{-\\frac{k}{8}e^{-10n/\\sqrt{\\kappa}}\\right\\},$ where the last step uses Eq. ( 25 ). ∎",
      "raw_span": {
        "byte_start_inclusive": 569382,
        "byte_end_exclusive": 595300,
        "start_line": 2750,
        "end_line": 2853,
        "raw_fragment_sha256": "58e9860006629df4e43aaff476528f1f466013746e94edcc75f9f174e84c6973"
      },
      "references": [],
      "disposition": "NODE"
    },
