    },
    {
      "atom_id": "A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1",
      "section": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "raw_locator": "#A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1",
      "source_text": "For every $\\bm{O}\\in O(n)^{k}$ , $A_{\\bm{O}}\\in\\mathcal{A}_{d,\\kappa}$ . The potential $f_{A_{\\bm{O}}}$ has unique minimizer $0$ and minimum value $0$ .",
      "raw_span": {
        "byte_start_inclusive": 596518,
        "byte_end_exclusive": 598182,
        "start_line": 2868,
        "end_line": 2871,
        "raw_fragment_sha256": "5f903e0d8a121b34cc860543046af918cc9e5732d42ea54e78c0ef475dbcc4dd"
      },
      "references": [],
      "disposition": "NODE"
    },
    {
      "atom_id": "A2.SS3.2",
      "section": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "proof-container",
      "raw_locator": "#A2.SS3.2",
      "source_text": "Proof of Lemma 3.4 . For $O\\in O(n)$ and $v\\in\\mathbb{R}^{n}$ , orthogonality gives $\\|Ov\\|=\\|v\\|$ . Hence, by Cauchy–Schwarz, $|\\langle v,Ov\\rangle|\\leq\\|v\\|^{2}$ . Since $v^{\\top}A_{O}v=\\frac{\\kappa+1}{2}\\|v\\|^{2}-\\frac{\\kappa-1}{2}\\langle v,Ov\\rangle,$ we obtain $\\|v\\|^{2}\\leq v^{\\top}A_{O}v\\leq\\kappa\\|v\\|^{2}$ . Together with $A_{O}=A_{O}^{\\top}$ , this proves $I_{n}\\preceq A_{O}\\preceq\\kappa I_{n}.$ (26) Now let $x=(x_{1},\\ldots,x_{k},z)\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ , where $x_{j}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{n}$ and $z\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d-kn}$ . Applying Eq. ( 26 ) to each block yields $\\displaystyle\\|x\\|^{2}$ $\\displaystyle=\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\\|x_{j}\\|^{2}+\\|z\\|^{2}$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\sum_{j=1}^{k}x_{j}^{\\top}A_{O_{j}}x_{j}+\\|z\\|^{2}=x^{\\top}A_{\\bm{O}}x$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\kappa\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\\|x_{j}\\|^{2}+\\|z\\|^{2}\\leq\\kappa\\|x\\|^{2}.$ The last inequality uses $\\kappa\\geq 1$ . When $kn=d$ , the terms involving $z$ are omitted. Since $A_{\\bm{O}}$ is symmetric, these inequalities imply $I_{d}\\preceq A_{\\bm{O}}\\preceq\\kappa I_{d}$ , and therefore $A_{\\bm{O}}\\in\\mathcal{A}_{d,\\kappa}$ . Finally, $f_{A_{\\bm{O}}}(0)=0$ , whereas for every $x\\neq 0$ , $f_{A_{\\bm{O}}}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}x^{\\top}A_{\\bm{O}}x\\geq\\frac{1}{2}\\|x\\|^{2}>0.$ Thus $0$ is the unique minimizer and the minimum value is $0$ . ∎",
      "raw_span": {
        "byte_start_inclusive": 598197,
        "byte_end_exclusive": 614482,
        "start_line": 2874,
        "end_line": 2940,
        "raw_fragment_sha256": "908290c92b7e3ff190de4053c2f7aeb4321ad09551ee1c7dd91bc1015538e97e"
      },
      "references": [],
      "disposition": "NODE"
    },
    {
      "atom_id": "A2.SS3::heading-3",
      "section": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "heading",
      "raw_locator": {
        "heading_text": "Proof of Lemma 3.4 .",
